{
  "id": "COMPOUND:30315 - PROTEIN:5702",
  "verbalization": "Hydroxy-Alpha-Sanshool is implicated in the regulation of CCF-STTG1 through a series of molecular interactions. The evidence suggests that Hydroxy-Alpha-Sanshool acts as a target for multiple compounds, including 6'-O-Z-Para-Methoxycinnamoylharpagide and (3aR,6S,6aR)-3,6-bis(3,4,5-trimethoxyphenyl)-1,3,3a,4,6,6a-hexahydrofuro[3,4-c]furan, all of which are known to target the CMP-N-acetylneuraminate-beta-1,4-galactoside alpha-2,3-sialyltransferase. This enzyme is a key player in sialylation, a process critical for cell surface glycosylation and immune function. The presence of multiple targets suggests a potential role for Hydroxy-Alpha-Sanshool in modulating the activity of this enzyme, which in turn could influence the function of CCF-STTG1. The integration of these pathways highlights a possible mechanism by which Hydroxy-Alpha-Sanshool may interact with CCF-STTG1, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be fully elucidated. The evidence supports a mechanistic link between Hydroxy-Alpha-Sanshool and CCF-STTG1, but further experimental validation is needed to confirm the direct relationship.",
